    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI made `householdId` deterministic from `(normalizedLastName, postcode)` and reworked household duplicate handling, keeping each touched function small and self-contained.\n\n**Centralized the household hash** (`OwnerIdentityKey.java`): `householdId(lastName, postcode)` now returns the first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode`, made `public`, and `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`) now composes it via postcode instead of address. This one helper is the single source everything else calls.\n\n**Pointed the three consumers at the helper** rather than duplicating the hash:\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 the `householdId` mapping expression now calls `OwnerIdentityKey.householdId(...)`.\n- `OwnerHouseholdSizeAdvice.java` \u2014 the household-size key (input to the membership tier) now uses the computed `householdId`.\n\n**Added the 409 block** (`OwnerHouseholdDuplicateAdvice.java`, new small advice): a second owner whose computed `householdId` already exists is rejected with 409, unless it sets `sharesHousehold`, which bypasses the block and creates it as a declared member. Modeled on the existing `OwnerPostcodeValidationAdvice`/`OwnerUniqueIdentityAdvice` pattern.\n\n**Stopped flagging declared members** (`OwnerPossibleDuplicateAdvice.java`): since a same-household owner is now either 409'd or a declared member, no created owner is a suspected duplicate \u2014 the advice simply records `possibleDuplicate=false`.\n\n**Schema** (`openapi.yml`): added the `sharesHousehold` input field and refreshed the `householdId`/`identityKey`/`possibleDuplicate` descriptions and examples.\n\nStructural impact was kept low by routing all three existing household computations through one new `public` helper (each change is a one-line delegation), putting the new 409 rule in its own tiny class rather than growing `OwnerUniqueIdentityAdvice`, and *shrinking* `OwnerPossibleDuplicateAdvice` (dropped its `ClinicService` dependency, the stream, and `softMatch`).",
